Our Hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure is well-suited to public and health procurement. We will break down the project into five phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run.

The key milestones and timelines are as follows:
- Framing phase (2 months): Define project scope, goals, and deliverables.
- Design phase (3 months): Design the AI solution, including the intelligent assistance tool and integration with existing systems.
- Pilot phase (6 months): Implement the solution in a limited perimeter, one or two departments, and test it with hospital staff.
- Generalisation phase (12 months): Roll out the solution to all services, providing training and support to staff.
- Run phase (48 months): Ensure the solution is operating correctly, provide maintenance and updates, and monitor its performance.

In terms of resource allocation, we will dedicate a project director, solution architect, two engineers, one data scientist, and a shared security compliance lead to this project. Additional resources for change management and training will be allocated as needed.

To ensure decision traceability, we will establish a joint steering committee with the client, meeting monthly, and an operational committee meeting fortnightly. We will also maintain a RACI matrix to document roles and responsibilities and have a single point of contact, the project director, for the client. A documented escalation path will be established to handle any issues that arise during the project.

Our past public sector references, such as the regional council and mutual health insurer projects, demonstrate our ability to deliver similar projects successfully. Our consortium partners, including OuraneCloud and Ligeo Santé, will provide expertise in French sovereign cloud hosting and health-IT integration, respectively. With our available capacity and governance practices, we are confident that we can deliver this project within the specified budget and timelines while ensuring decision traceability and meeting the client's requirements.
